          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %strong Homotopy totalizations
            are a special case of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+simplices"} category of simplices
          %p
            Homotopy totalizations can be defined in any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+category"} relative category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structures"} model structures
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+categories"} enriched model categories
            are the most common setup.
          %h2#computation Computation
          %p
            In any
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+model+category"} enriched model category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+object"} cosimplicial object
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\colon \Delta\to C
          %p
            can be computed in three different ways, all of which use the notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+end"} enriched end
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functors"} enriched functors
            (i.e.,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limits"} weighted limits
          %p
            Specifically, consider the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mi Δ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi op
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom\colon (V^\Delta)^{op} \times C^\Delta \to C
          %p
            that takes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+end"} enriched end
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+limit"} weighted limit
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
            over which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is enriched.
          %p
            If we set the first argument to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constant+functor"} constant functor
            with value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+unit"} monoidal unit
            of
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit+functor"} limit functor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\Delta\to C
          %p
            The functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom
            becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+Quillen+bifunctor"} right Quillen bifunctor
            if we equip
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^\Delta
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mi Δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\Delta
            with one of the three following pairs of model structures:
          %ul
            %li injective and injective;
            %li projective and projective;
            %li Reedy and Reedy.
          %p
            Accordingly, the homotopy totalization of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+object"} cosimplicial object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\colon \Delta\to C
            can be computed as follows.
          %ul
            %li
              Cofibrantly resolve the constant weight
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              in one of the three model structures listed above.
            %li
              Fibrantly resolve
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              in the other model structure in the same pair.
            %li
              Compute
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Hom
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Q
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi R
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(Q 1, R X)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            Cofibrant resolutions in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+model+structure"} injective model structure
            can be computed by appling some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution+functor"} cofibrant resolution functor
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            objectwise.
          %p
            Cofibrant resolutions in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
            can be computed inductively, by repeatedly factoring the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/latching+map"} latching map
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"} cofibration
            followed by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalence"} weak equivalence
            and adjusting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            accordingly.
          %p
            Cofibrant resolutions in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure"} projective model structure
            can be computed explicitly in some practical examples.
          %h3#reduction_to_semisimplicial_objects Reduction to semisimplicial objects
          %p
            The inclusion of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+semisimplices"} category of semisimplices
            (i.e., fininite inhabited totally ordered sets and injective order-preserving maps) into the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+simplices"} category of simplices
            (with the injectivity condition dropped) is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+initial+functor"} homotopy initial functor
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
          %p
            Thus, homotopy totalizations can be computed as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
            over the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+semisimplices"} category of semisimplices
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+category"} direct category
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#simplicial_sets Simplicial sets
          %p
            A Reedy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+replacement"} cofibrant replacement
            of the constant weight
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\colon \Delta\to sSet
            can be computed as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mi Δ
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_\Delta\colon\Delta\to sSet
          %p Thus, the homotopy totalization of
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi sSet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\colon \Delta \to sSet
          %p can be computed as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Y
                    %mi Δ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(Y_\Delta, R X),
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R X
            is the Reedy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+replacement"} fibrant replacement
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h3#chain_complexes_of_abelian_groups Chain complexes of abelian groups
          %p
            For
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            (which we equip with the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} projective model structure on chain complexes
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} N
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ch
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{N} \mathbf{Z} [-]\colon \Delta \to Ch,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{N}
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalized+chains+functor"} normalized chains functor
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Z}[-]
            denotes the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+simplicial+abelian+group+functor"} free simplicial abelian group functor
          %p
            All
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+objects"} cosimplicial objects
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            are Reedy fibrant because the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matching+map"} matching map
            is a degreewise surjection of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
          %p
            Thus, the homotopy totalization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ch
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\colon \Delta \to Ch
            can be computed as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} N
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\mathrm{N} \mathbf{Z} [-], X),
          %p
            which is isomorphic to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product"} direct product
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+complex"} total complex
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+chain+complex"} double chain complex
            obtained by applying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold%E2%80%93Kan+correspondence"} Dold–Kan correspondence
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+object"} cosimplicial object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo →
                    %mi Ch
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\colon \Delta\to Ch
          %h3#topological_spaces Topological spaces
          %p
            Consider
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalences"} weak homotopy equivalences
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+model+structure"} Serre model structure
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+simplex"} topological simplex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Δ
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\Delta}\colon \Delta\to Top
            is Reedy cofibrant as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+topological+space"} cosimplicial topological space
          %p
            Not all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+objects"} cosimplicial objects
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            are Reedy
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant"} fibrant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matching+map"} matching map
            need not be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre+fibration+of+topological+spaces"} Serre fibration of topological spaces
          %p
            However, we can pass to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimplicial"} semisimplicial
            setting, as explained above. In this, case Reedy fibrancy boils down to the objectwise fibrancy, which is always true for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
          %p
            Thus, the homotopy totalization of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X\colon \Delta \to Top
            can be computed as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Δ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(\mathbf{\Delta}, X)
          %p
            in the category of functors
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi inj
                    %mo →
                    %mi Top
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{inj}\to Top
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fat+geometric+realization"} fat geometric realization
            = succeed "." do
              %strong fat geometric totalization
